{"parentUuid":"dbc6d751-5302-4fce-aad6-c3cd761bb764","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6c9c6e35-cbf1-4fca-aec8-11abd6a40819","agentId":"a320534075171177a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013UMNJ3aDz4vKWJ5vW8No4D","type":"tool_result","content":"### Notes\n- Human task: not for agents.\n- Never paste a key into an agent prompt or an issue.\n\nIN FLIGHT\n  nothing else in progress\nOVERLAPS\n  none: no open PR touches .env, docs/hack/BRIEF.md\nNEXT STEPS\n  1. context: entire search \"<topic>\", entire graph query, entire brain brief\n  2. small commits; stage files by name (git add path/to/file), never git add -A\n  3. ./hq check before every push\n  4. write .context/pr-8.md, then ./hq pr 8 --agent claude --body-file .context/pr-8.md\n  stuck: ./hq release 8 --agent claude --needs-human --note \"<why>\"\n45:## Hour-one sign-ups\n46-Start these at kick-off; each can take hours or days.\n47-- Street Manager open data registration (SNS subscription must be confirmed within 3 days;\n48-  fallback: a recorded sample of Newcastle permits).\n49-- Gemini paid tier (billing enabled on the key).\n50-- Hotel affiliate network (Awin, CJ, Expedia, Travelpayouts). Expect no approval during the event;\n51-  the demo uses placeholder links.\n52-- Apple developer account and HealthKit entitlement; test Watch signing, stop at hour 2.\n53-- Check which Observatory noise sensors reported in the last 24 hours; backfill 30+ nights.\n54-\n55-## Risks\n56-| Risk | Likelihood | Fallback |\n57-|---|---|---|\n58-| Watch app signing eats hours | High | Stop at hour 2; the phone reads Watch data through HealthKit anyway |\n59-| HealthKit entitlement or developer account not ready | Medium | Sort it in hour one; worst case, export Health data from the Health app and import it |\n60-| iOS stops recording when locked | Medium | Test on the first evening; fallback is screen-on with Guided Access |\n61-| Nobody sleeps near an Observatory sensor | Happened (confirmed 2026-11-14) | The personal night still works; the city map uses sensors near the venue |\n62-| Street Manager feed not live in time | Medium | A recorded sample of Newcastle permits |\n63-| Observatory sensors stale or API down | Medium | History backfilled into Tiger in hour one; pick sensors that reported in the last 24 hours |\n64-| Gemini paid tier not set up | Low | Enable billing in hour one |\n65-| Hotel affiliate access not granted | High | OpenStreetMap hotels with placeholder booking links |\n66-| Live audio fails in a loud hall | Medium | Speaker held against the phone; backup video |\n67-| Judges challenge the causation claim | High | Counts against the random-window baseline; say \"linked to\", never \"caused by\" |\n68-\n69-## Constraints\n70-- MLH rules: only work done during the event is judged.\n71-- This framework (`hq`, agent rules, docs, GitHub templates) is pre-event tooling, prepared before\n72-  DurHack and disclosed in `README.md`. The submission repo is created from it at kick-off and\n73-  all product code is written during the event.\n74-- Secrets live in `.env` only. Never commit them or paste them into an agent prompt.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f54b6d0d-82dc-47e5-a4b1-39539095fd94","timestamp":"2026-11-14T22:55:02.177Z","sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbc6d751-5302-4fce-aad6-c3cd761bb764","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/Users/nick/conductor/repos/durhack-proj/.claude/worktrees/agent-a320534075171177a","sessionId":"736d853a-59a1-497e-9c09-03efc1099979","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"docs/event-times-devnet"}
